  "final_answer": "<think>\n\n</think>\n\n- **Retry Rounds:** Retry logic in LLM agents can lead to repeated context processing if not managed with graph-aware tracking of execution history.  \n- **Debugging Loops:** Debugging loops often involve repeated tool calls and context reprocessing, which can be mitigated with structured working memory and state tracking.  \n- **Repeated Context/History:** Agents may reprocess outdated or redundant context from prior steps, increasing prefill token usage and computational cost.  \n- **Prefill Tokens:** Graph-aware context management can reduce redundant prefill by efficiently tracking and reusing only relevant context, avoiding unnecessary token consumption.",
